{"name":"Parfait","hex":"#c8a6a1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Parfait","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from French [in turn transferred from the nickname]."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Parfait"}],"entries":[{"title":"Parfait","blocks":[{"text":"Parfait is either of two types of dessert. In France, where the dish originated, parfait is made by boiling cream, egg, sugar and syrup to create a custard-like or meringue-like puree which is then frozen. The American version consists of layers differentiated by the inclusion of such ingredients as granola, nuts, yogurt and liqueurs, topped off with fruits or whipped cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Parfait_samples_by_pinguino_in_Osaka%2C_Japan.jpg/330px-Parfait_samples_by_pinguino_in_Osaka%2C_Japan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parfait","wikidata":"Q13314"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Parfait_glac%C3%A9_au_Grand_Marnier%2C_fruits_confits_et_pain_d%27%C3%A9pice.JPG/500px-Parfait_glac%C3%A9_au_Grand_Marnier%2C_fruits_confits_et_pain_d%27%C3%A9pice.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Parfait_glac%C3%A9_au_Grand_Marnier%2C_fruits_confits_et_pain_d%27%C3%A9pice.JPG/1280px-Parfait_glac%C3%A9_au_Grand_Marnier%2C_fruits_confits_et_pain_d%27%C3%A9pice.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Parfait_glac%C3%A9_au_Grand_Marnier%2C_fruits_confits_et_pain_d%27%C3%A9pice.JPG/500px-Parfait_glac%C3%A9_au_Grand_Marnier%2C_fruits_confits_et_pain_d%27%C3%A9pice.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"French parfait","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/